    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42641" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sarīsa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-issa</span></b> ), ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρισα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A long Macedonian lance</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
			19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 42</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">38, 7</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 7, 4, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 7, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				466</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 479 al.</span></i>; cf. Fest. pp. 145 and
			251.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, in gen., for <i>Macedonians</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 8, 298</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 47</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">denominatio est ...si quis Macedonas appellarit
					hoc modo: Non tam cito sarissae Graecia potiti sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 32, 43</span></i>
			.</div>
